  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A rectangle is inscribed in a circle with a diameter lying along the line <math><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the two adjacent vertices of the rectangle are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then the area of the rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>in sq. units<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is:",
    "image": null
  },
